.nh
.TH "PVEFORGE" "1" "Sep 2026" "pveforge" "pveforge manual"

.SH NAME
pveforge-storage-create - Create a storage definition, idempotently, refusing a differing one


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpveforge storage create <target-id> <name> --type <type> [--data key=value ...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a cluster-wide PVE storage definition (POST /storage), idempotently.

.PP
The definition is type-agnostic: --type names the storage type and every
other parameter is a raw --data key=value, passed to PVE unchanged (PVE
validates them and its error text propagates verbatim), exactly like
`vm create`\&'s raw create fields. One small guard runs client-side
before any POST: a type with a known required key missing is refused early
(v1: --type zfspool needs --data pool=<zpool>, or the storage comes up
inactive).

.PP
A storage definition is CLUSTER-WIDE, not node-scoped: it is written to the
cluster's storage.cfg whichever node's API is addressed. Creating one needs
Datastore.Allocate at /storage (datacenter) — a storage pool token with only
Datastore.AllocateSpace cannot create a definition, only allocate volumes
within one.

.PP
Idempotent:
  - absent            -> created;
  - present, matching -> no-op (nothing changed);
  - present, differing-> REFUSED, with a desired-vs-actual diff and NO write;
    a future \fBstorage set\fR is the way to converge one deliberately.
--force re-POSTs a present+matching storage instead of no-opping (PVE then
refuses the duplicate), but STILL refuses a differing definition.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--data\fP=[]
	a raw PVE create parameter, key=value (repeatable): pool=..., content=..., nodes=...

.PP
\fB--force\fP[=false]
	re-POST even if the storage already matches (PVE refuses the duplicate); still refuses a differing definition

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--lock-wait\fP=0s
	how long to wait for another pveforge process's lock on this object before giving up (0 = the 15m0s default; at most 1h0m0s). The default exceeds the 10m0s ceiling on waiting for a PVE task because a legitimate lock holder may be in such a wait the whole time

.PP
\fB--roster\fP=""
	path to the roster file (overrides PVEFORGE_ROSTER and the default ./pveforge.toml)

.PP
\fB--type\fP=""
	the PVE storage type to create (zfspool, dir, lvmthin, nfs, ...); required


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpveforge-storage(1)\fP
